# Immutable caching for assets that never change without a filename change.
# Fixes Chrome's "preloaded but not used" warnings on repeat views: with the
# Pages default (max-age=0, must-revalidate) every font preload triggered a
# revalidation whose response was never consumed.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# CSP scope audited A4-5; re-audited 2026-08-12 when analytics was ported from
# the live WordPress site and Calendly was retired.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A TAG IN GTM. A strict CSP and a tag manager are in
# tension: GTM can inject any vendor it likes, but the browser will silently
# block anything whose origin is not listed here. The console shows a CSP
# violation, the tag simply never fires, and GTM's own UI reports success. If a
# new tag ever looks live in GTM but dead in the vendor's dashboard, this file
# is the first place to look.
#
# Every origin below maps to a verified dependency:
#   googletagmanager.com    — gtm.js container loader + the no-JS ns.html iframe
#                             (src/components/Analytics.astro)
#   google-analytics.com    — GA4 collect endpoint (connect) plus legacy pixel
#                             fallback (img); region1.* needs the wildcard.
#                             Two properties: G-696ZEHHK32 and G-FXS0D8YFKQ
#   googleadservices.com    — Google Ads AW-16860441463 conversion script
#   doubleclick.net         — ad.doubleclick.net/ccm/s/collect (connect), plus
#                             conversion pixel (img) and linker iframe (frame)
#   gstatic.com             — wcm/loader.js and call-tracking_9.js. This is
#                             Google Ads WEBSITE CALL METRICS: it rewrites phone
#                             numbers on the page to a Google forwarding number.
#                             The site's real number lives in constants.ts, so if
#                             a displayed number ever disagrees with that file,
#                             this tag is why — it is not a bug in the build.
#   google.com              — Ads conversion pixel fallback
#   connect.facebook.net    — Meta Pixel 705778782363299 (fbevents.js)
#   facebook.com            — Meta Pixel tr/ collection endpoint
#   clarity.ms              — Microsoft Clarity project qtb32zg360; c.bing.com is
#                             Clarity's secondary collector
#   deepriverdigital.com    — DRD first-party tracker (drd-track.js + /ingest)
#   cloudflareinsights.com  — Cloudflare Web Analytics RUM beacon. NOT added by
#                             this repo: Cloudflare injects beacon.min.js into
#                             the response automatically, so it appeared the
#                             moment the site went live on the production domain
#                             and was blocked on day one (2026-08-17). Turning
#                             Web Analytics off in the Cloudflare dashboard is
#                             the alternative to allowing it here.
#   usebasin.com            — form-action for the careers and lead forms
#
# 'unsafe-inline' is required twice over: Astro emits every page script as an
# inline <script type="module">, and GTM's loader plus any Custom HTML tag are
# inline too. 'unsafe-eval' is NOT required — no eval or new Function in dist/.
#
# upgrade-insecure-requests is not decorative: Google's call-tracking tag
# requests http://www.gstatic.com/call-tracking/call-tracking_9.js over plain
# HTTP (observed 2026-08-12). Without the upgrade that is blocked as mixed
# content on the HTTPS production site.
#
# The origin list above was built by loading a real build and reading
# performance.getEntriesByType('resource') — not from the vendors' docs. Redo
# that after any container change; GA4 in particular sends some hits via
# navigator.sendBeacon, which does NOT appear in resource timing, so the
# google-analytics.com entries are kept on documentation rather than observation.
#
# 2026-08-13 — connect-src was too narrow and PageSpeed on the pages.dev deploy
# caught five blocked collection calls that resource timing had missed. Google
# Ads and GA4 do not collect on the hosts that serve their scripts:
#   www.google.com/ccm/collect, /rmkt/collect  — Ads conversion + remarketing
#   www.googleadservices.com/pagead/conversion/…/wcm  — call-tracking conversion
#   stats.g.doubleclick.net/g/collect                 — GA4 Signals
# All five are now allowed. This was NOT cosmetic: every Google Ads conversion
# on the site was being dropped by the browser while GTM reported success —
# exactly the silent-failure mode warned about at the top of this file.
# *.google.com is deliberately broad: Ads collects on regional ccTLDs for some
# visitors, and enumerating them is impractical.
#
# Calendly origins were removed when the scheduler was archived. If you ever
# restore src/components/_archive/CalendlyCta.astro you must also add back:
#   script-src/style-src/img-src https://assets.calendly.com
#   frame-src https://calendly.com https://*.calendly.com
#
# GTM Preview mode needs https://tagmanager.google.com and Google's font/style
# origins, which are deliberately NOT allowed here. Debug against a preview
# deploy expecting Preview to be partially blocked, or verify via the vendor
# dashboards (GA4 Realtime, Clarity, Meta Events Manager) instead.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), autoplay=(self), fullscreen=(self), picture-in-picture=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: upgrade-insecure-requests; default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://www.gstatic.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://connect.facebook.net https://www.clarity.ms https://*.clarity.ms https://track.deepriverdigital.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.google.com https://www.gstatic.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://ad.doubleclick.net https://www.facebook.com https://*.facebook.com https://*.clarity.ms; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://www.google.com https://*.google.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://ad.doubleclick.net https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://stats.g.doubleclick.net https://*.g.doubleclick.net https://*.clarity.ms https://c.bing.com https://connect.facebook.net https://track.deepriverdigital.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://*.cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://td.doubleclick.net https://ad.doubleclick.net; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self' https://usebasin.com;
